#
# Talisman, the owner's Player Card: layer 76 of the matrix. It reads
# zxvd's player.card (sicily.h S2/S3) and shows the tier the measured
# inputs earn, each input with its source, how far each has come toward
# the next tier's threshold, whether that tier is earned, and the perks.
# An input zxvd reports as 0 (bond, uptime and giving have no source on a
# node yet, and zxvd says why) is shown as missing with that reason, never
# as met. The history of tiers is kept in the C model (talisman_model.h
# TM4). Read only.
#
# Tiers give no priority, discount or credit, as player.card says; the
# card never implies otherwise, and every notice says so (TM3).
#
# 5 later layers lean on this one, so its entries are general rules owned
# here (CONCEPTS.tsv): how far a value has come toward a threshold, held
# at the threshold, and whether every value meets its threshold, as a
# truth and as a number. Nothing nearer the core fits: the shared blocks
# are capacities, shares, days and gcds; used_share.used_x100 refuses a
# value past its total, which a met threshold often is; Coffer's entries
# are money, and a tier is no money; Wellspring's goal progress is not
# held at the goal, and Wellspring (layer 89) is built after this layer,
# so it may not be used here. Kitling, Ninefold and Vintner, which the
# task names, are not built yet.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind, since a witnessed call compares answers
# exactly and a truth entry refuses a number (zxapp.c run_one B3). Eve
# answers truths only (zxapp_eve.c EV2), and Trebago answers numbers, so
# the task's "Eve + Trebago" for the tier earned is split as Gatehouse
# splits its rule: Eve and KRON witness the truth (earned), Trebago and
# KRON the number (earned_n), and the model's C is the third witness of
# both (talisman_rules.h). Eve checks each field against its own range
# alone, so every input comes as its margin, what it has minus what the
# tier needs.
#
# Planned languages: Eiffel (design by contract) and Solidity (contract
# rules) own the tier rule, earned; RPG (reports from fixed records) owns
# the card's progress figures, reach_x100. None runs yet; Eve, KRON,
# Trebago and Sutra stand in.
zxapp 1
id     talisman
name   Talisman
version 1.0.0
slot   76
layer  L1
matrix 76
icon   icons/l1/076-talisman.svg
budget 233
needs  ledger.read
needs  sys.read
model  apps/talisman_model.c

# How far an input has come toward its threshold, x100, held at 10000
# (met), floored (TL1): Sutra divides and holds 9(9), Trebago counts the
# floor exactly; a need of 0, a negative or a value past 9(9) is refused
# by Sutra and answered by Trebago: held.
provides reach_x100 num have need
logic    sutra   reach_x100 apps/blocks/talisman/reach.sutra
logic    trebago reach_x100 apps/blocks/talisman/reach.tb
pending  RPG reach_x100

# The next tier earned (TL2): every margin at or above 0, uptime's at most
# 10000 bps. Eve declares the ranges, KRON reads any margin at or above 0
# as met: an uptime margin past 10000 is held.
provides earned truth cred bond uptime
logic    eve  earned apps/blocks/talisman/earned.eve
logic    kron earned apps/blocks/talisman/earned.kron
pending  Eiffel earned
pending  Solidity earned

# The same rule as a number to count with, 1 or 0 (TL3): Trebago holds
# the ranges, KRON reads any margin at or above 0 as met: held past them.
provides earned_n num cred bond uptime
logic    trebago earned_n apps/blocks/talisman/earned_n.tb
logic    kron    earned_n apps/blocks/talisman/earned_n.kron

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check reach_x100 have=0,50,100,150,1,2,999999999,0,10001 need=100,100,100,100,3,3,999999999,1,10000 = 0,5000,10000,10000,3333,6666,10000,0,10000
check reach_x100 have=1,1 need=1,0 = both
check reach_x100 have=1,1000000000 need=1,1 = both
check earned cred=0,5,0,0,-1,0,0,999999999999999999 bond=0,0,7,0,0,-1,0,0 uptime=0,0,0,10000,0,0,-1,0 = true,true,true,true,false,false,false,true
check earned cred=0,0 bond=0,0 uptime=0,10001 = both
check earned_n cred=0,5,0,0,-1,0,0,999999999999999999 bond=0,0,7,0,0,-1,0,0 uptime=0,0,0,10000,0,0,-1,0 = 1,1,1,1,0,0,0,1
check earned_n cred=0,0 bond=0,0 uptime=0,10001 = both
